WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.936
-My first guest is an NBA legend

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:05.304
and a co-owner
of the Los Angeles Dodgers.

00:00:05.304 --> 00:00:08.274
Here is the one and only
Magic Johnson!

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:09.275
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:11.244
Yeah! That's what
I'm talking about!

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:12.845
Hey, bud!

00:00:12.845 --> 00:00:14.447
Magic Johnson!

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:16.516
Oh, it's great to see you, bud.
Welcome.

00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:18.250
-And you, too, Jimmy.
How you doing, man?

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:20.686
-I'm doing good, pal.
I want to ask you,

00:00:20.686 --> 00:00:22.755
'cause you have
one of the greatest nicknames

00:00:22.755 --> 00:00:25.391
in the history of sports.

00:00:25.391 --> 00:00:28.294
But you also had a nickname
before it was Magic Johnson.

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:30.163
You were June Bug Johnson.

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:32.098
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:35.468
-Why is that?
Why were you June Bug Johnson?

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:37.403
-Well, you know, my parents
are from the South.

00:00:37.403 --> 00:00:39.672
And when you're from the South,

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:42.008
everybody, especially
if you're African-American,

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:46.946
you get -- Every male is like
one June Bug in every family.

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:50.083
So I was the June Bug
of our family.

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:52.018
You know, I have six sisters
and three brothers.

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:54.687
So they happened
to give it to me.

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:58.324
-How did -- And then a sports
writer called you Magic?

00:00:58.324 --> 00:00:59.725
-Yes.

00:00:59.725 --> 00:01:03.996
When I went to high school,
my ninth game of the season,

00:01:03.996 --> 00:01:07.066
my first year of high school,
I was 15 years old.

00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:11.204
And we went to play a school,
and we blew them out.

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:12.972
They were a powerhouse
in the state of Michigan.

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:18.144
I had 38 points, 16 rebounds,
and 15 assists.

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:20.079
That was my first triple double.

00:01:20.079 --> 00:01:21.881
And the guy came in and said,

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:23.883
"Somebody's already
called Dr. J.

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:25.417
Somebody's already called Big E.

00:01:25.417 --> 00:01:27.153
I want to call you Magic."

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:28.888
And, you know, hey, Jimmy,

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:31.557
I said, "No way
this is going to stick."

00:01:31.557 --> 00:01:34.493
And all the brothers
in the neighbor, you know,

00:01:34.493 --> 00:01:37.263
they were like, "Man, we not
gonna call you no Magic."

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:38.331
You know?

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:39.699
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:41.000
-Yeah, you're June Bug, man.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.201
Come on.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:01:42.201 --> 00:01:43.403
-It's not going to stick.

00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:45.071
And now here you are.
There's no one else.

00:01:45.071 --> 00:01:46.639
You can't call
anyone else Magic.

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:49.542
-That's right. I'm wrong,
and the sports writer was right.

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:51.177
I've been Magic ever since.

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:52.545
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:54.614
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:54.614 --> 00:01:56.549
-I want to talk to you about
the summer Olympics coming up.

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:59.185
We're coming up
on the 30th anniversary

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:02.755
of what is know as the greatest
basketball team in history,

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:05.424
the 1992 Dream Team.

00:02:05.424 --> 00:02:07.493
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:07.493 --> 00:02:11.230
Now, at this point,
you and Larry Bird were rivals

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:13.899
for almost two decades.

00:02:13.899 --> 00:02:15.468
And now you're teammates.

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:17.703
What was that like?

00:02:17.703 --> 00:02:19.339
-Well, Jimmy,
it was on my bucket list

00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:21.040
to play with Larry Bird one day,

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.808
play with Michael Jordan
one day.

00:02:22.808 --> 00:02:24.009
And here it is.

00:02:24.009 --> 00:02:26.979
I get a chance on the Dream Team
to do just that.

00:02:26.979 --> 00:02:29.648
And it was great
to play with Larry.

00:02:29.648 --> 00:02:31.518
We had been rivals.
We hated each other.

00:02:31.518 --> 00:02:36.955
We played against each other
in the NCAA championship game.

00:02:36.955 --> 00:02:39.992
And so I had to take the Birdman
down in that game,

00:02:39.992 --> 00:02:41.527
and then --
-[ Laughing ] Oh, my God.

00:02:41.527 --> 00:02:44.097
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.097 --> 00:02:45.765
You're going to get in trouble
again, man.

00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:48.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:49.402
You took the Birdman down.

00:02:49.402 --> 00:02:51.637
-And then we played three times
in the NBA,

00:02:51.637 --> 00:02:53.840
and my Lakers won two
and he won one.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:55.808
But I would say this --

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:59.145
There's nobody
that I ever played against

00:02:59.145 --> 00:03:02.048
that I loved and respected
more than Larry Bird.

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:04.951
The man -- Listen, you couldn't
give him a inch,

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:08.154
or he would just shoot it
right in your face.

00:03:08.154 --> 00:03:10.222
He was dominant
at both ends of the court.

00:03:10.222 --> 00:03:13.058
And so Larry Bird
made me a better player,

00:03:13.058 --> 00:03:14.894
and I think I made him
a better player.

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:17.730
And together,
we made the NBA better.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.865
-That's right you did.
That's right.

00:03:19.865 --> 00:03:21.834
Absolutely. Good man.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:24.737
If you took the 1992 Dream Team

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:28.541
and put them up against a team
of today's best NBA players --

00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:31.777
LeBron, Durant,
James Harden, Steph Curry.

00:03:31.777 --> 00:03:33.379
-Hey, let me cut you off.

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:36.048
It don't matter who you put.
We gon' beat them.

00:03:36.048 --> 00:03:39.285
-What?!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:41.553
And by how much? By how much?

00:03:41.553 --> 00:03:44.090
-You know, really,
it really don't matter

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:47.360
as long as you win, right?
And so --

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:48.627
-Why?
-They're the Dream Team.

00:03:48.627 --> 00:03:51.830
Listen, man. That team --
We had everything.

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:55.568
Everything that you want in a
basketball team, we had, right?

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:57.903
We could shoot from the outside.

00:03:57.903 --> 00:03:59.872
We could dominate you inside.

00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:01.574
We played great defense.

00:04:01.574 --> 00:04:03.475
I mean, when you got
Scottie Pippen

00:04:03.475 --> 00:04:06.679
and Michael Jordan
on those wings like that --

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:08.047
And then David Robinson

00:04:08.047 --> 00:04:10.916
and Patrick Ewing,
who was dominant at that time.

00:04:10.916 --> 00:04:14.653
I mean, and Charles Barkley,
who was unbelievable.

00:04:14.653 --> 00:04:17.090
You know, we had the best
players in the world --

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:19.458
Karl Malone, John Stockton,

00:04:19.458 --> 00:04:21.660
Chris Mullin,
a New Yorker, Chris Mullin...

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:23.495
-That's right, Chris Mullin.
-...Clyde Drexler.

00:04:23.495 --> 00:04:24.664
It's an amazing team.

00:04:24.664 --> 00:04:26.232
-Speaking of Patrick Ewing,

00:04:26.232 --> 00:04:28.634
can you believe what's going on
with the Knicks?

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:30.770
-Oh.
-Whoo! Yo!

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:31.837
[ Applause ]

00:04:31.837 --> 00:04:33.639
-Let me just say this.

00:04:33.639 --> 00:04:37.042
The Knicks are on
a nine-game winning streak.

00:04:37.042 --> 00:04:40.179
They have the coach of the year
in Coach Thibodeau.

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:42.848
Julius Randle has been
a dominant player.

00:04:42.848 --> 00:04:45.418
He should make the all-NBA team.
-Yep.

00:04:45.418 --> 00:04:47.953
-The League is better when
the New York Knicks are better,

00:04:47.953 --> 00:04:51.457
and I'm so excited
for Knicks fans.

00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:54.494
I'm excited for the NBA,
and I tell you what --

00:04:54.494 --> 00:04:58.064
This is the one problem, Jimmy,
everybody's going to have.

00:04:58.064 --> 00:05:00.266
Nobody in the NBA in the East

00:05:00.266 --> 00:05:02.101
is going to want to play
the Knicks in the playoffs.

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:03.302
I'll tell that you right now.

00:05:03.302 --> 00:05:04.537
-That's right. Really?

00:05:04.537 --> 00:05:06.205
I love hearing that.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:06.205 --> 00:05:08.307
-Yeah, because they play defense

00:05:08.307 --> 00:05:10.476
better than anybody
in the League.

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:11.778
And they're tough.

00:05:11.778 --> 00:05:13.845
And they're mentally
and physically tough.

00:05:13.845 --> 00:05:17.015
I like the way Coach Thibodeau
has the guys playing.

00:05:17.015 --> 00:05:20.786
-So, who do you pick --
the team to go all the way?

00:05:20.786 --> 00:05:24.156
-Well, I think you got to still
put Brooklyn as the favorite,

00:05:24.156 --> 00:05:26.992
as well as the Lakers
on the West.

00:05:26.992 --> 00:05:30.963
And I would love to see
that match-up in the NBA finals.

00:05:30.963 --> 00:05:32.698
-Come on, Knicks.
-And let's see what happens.

00:05:32.698 --> 00:05:34.199
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:34.199 --> 00:05:36.902
I want to ask you about this,
'cause you're one of the owners

00:05:36.902 --> 00:05:39.438
of the Dodgers,
the L.A. Dodgers.

00:05:39.438 --> 00:05:41.707
And they just won
the championship.

00:05:41.707 --> 00:05:44.009
You've been a winner
so many times.

00:05:44.009 --> 00:05:47.913
What does it feel like to be a
winner as an owner in baseball?

00:05:47.913 --> 00:05:49.281
-It's different, right?

00:05:49.281 --> 00:05:51.350
Because as a player,

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:53.619
you can control
what happens on the court.

00:05:53.619 --> 00:05:57.456
But as an owner,
it drives you absolutely crazy

00:05:57.456 --> 00:05:59.125
because you can't control

00:05:59.125 --> 00:06:01.394
anything that happens
on the field.

00:06:01.394 --> 00:06:03.596
We've been to the World Series
three times,

00:06:03.596 --> 00:06:05.998
and we finally won
this past season.

00:06:05.998 --> 00:06:10.536
I'm happy for all my -- the
players and the L.A. fan base,

00:06:10.536 --> 00:06:12.871
because the Lakers
end up winning,

00:06:12.871 --> 00:06:15.140
and the Dodgers won
in the same year.

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:18.344
So it's been a great year
for Laker fans and Dodger fans

00:06:18.344 --> 00:06:19.778
and L.A. as a community.

00:06:19.778 --> 00:06:21.280
-That's right. Good man.

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:22.648
I -- It's all you.

00:06:22.648 --> 00:06:25.551
You're the secret.
You're the secret, buddy.

00:06:25.551 --> 00:06:26.719
-Thank you, my man.

